@title Course Completion Summary
@subtitle Online and blended courses, Fall 2024 to Spring 2026, for the academic senate meeting on 2026-11-10
@author Dr. Aaliyah Brandt, Institutional Research
@date 2026-11-10

# Completion at a glance

kpi Completion rate, Spring 2026 | 79.0% | +9 pts in four terms | good

kpi Enrolled, Spring 2026 | 1,502 | +262 vs Fall 2024 | good
kpi Completed, Spring 2026 | 1,187
kpi Biggest jump | +5 pts | Fall 2025
kpi Online vs in person | -17.9 pts | 68.1% vs 86.0% | bad

Completion is up 9 points in four terms, from 70.0% in Fall 2024 to 79.0% in Spring 2026. The biggest single jump, 5 points, came in Fall 2025, when free tutoring for first-year students started on 2025-08-25. Online courses still complete about 18 points below in-person ones.

# Term by term

data terms = term,enrolled,completed,rate; Fall 2024,1240,868,70.0; Spring 2025,1315,947,72.0; Fall 2025,1410,1086,77.0; Spring 2026,1502,1187,79.0

chart line terms x=term y=rate unit=% labels mark="Fall 2025 tutoring" title="Completion rate by term"

table terms title="Enrollment and completion by term"

# By format, Spring 2026

data formats = format,enrolled,completed,rate; In person,520,447,86.0; Hybrid,600,480,80.0; Online,382,260,68.1

chart hbar formats x=format y=rate unit=% focus="Online" labels title="Completion rate by format, Spring 2026"

table formats

Online is the format with the most room to improve: at 68.1% it completes about 18 points below in person (86.0%) and 12 points below hybrid (80.0%).

# Notes

! **Completed** means a passing grade, not attendance.

! Withdrawals before the census date, the 15th day of the term, are not counted as enrolled.

- Free tutoring for first-year students began on 2025-08-25, at the start of Fall 2025.
